# Context-Hub Environment Variables
# ============================================================
# This file is a quick-start guide. The actual per-profile templates live in:
#
#   context_hub/_env_examples/.env.example.quickstart   — SQLite + mock + memory scheduler
#   context_hub/_env_examples/.env.example.personal     — SQLite + BGE-M3 + sqlite scheduler
#   context_hub/_env_examples/.env.example.production   — PostgreSQL + live ingest
#
# Pick the profile that matches your setup, copy it to .env, and fill in any
# REQUIRED fields. Then start the server with:
#
#   context-hub serve
#
# NEVER commit .env (it is in .gitignore). Only commit .env.example files.
# Treat secret values (Slack tokens, Gmail OAuth tokens, API keys) like passwords.
# ============================================================
